# The image only needs the entrypoint script copied in at build time —
# everything else (config, skills, workspace, agent state, logs) is
# bind-mounted at runtime, not baked into the image. Excluding it all
# from the build context also avoids Docker choking on root-owned
# runtime directories (logs/, state/, credentials/, etc.) that the
# container creates on previous runs.
**
!docker-entrypoint.sh
